{"id":"u-5c0ea4d3-f497-47f4-993c-d5103b426a2e","src":"community","title":"5/3/1 Valkyrie Protocol","author":"Mithosphere","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/TRc58C-531-valkyrie-protocol","desc":"The Valkyrie Protocol is a strength and hypertrophy template built explicitly on Jim Wendler’s 5/3/1 principles, tailored for female lifters who want to build a strong, balanced, hourglass physique without spending half their day in the gym.\n\nToo many female-focused programs rely on endless low-load activation movements, random circuit training, or high-fatigue variations that burn calories but fail to build lasting muscle and strength. This program shifts the focus back to structural progressive overload and basic hard work, using a highly efficient training layout that guarantees you are in and out of the gym in under an hour.\n\nWHO IS THIS PROGRAM FOR\nThis template is built for intermediate female lifters who want a structured, reliable method to increase their compound strength and build an elite aesthetic footprint. \n\nThe architecture of the program is built on three core pillars:\n\n1. 5's PROGRESSION (5PRO)\nTo eliminate central nervous system exhaustion and protect your training consistency, all primary compound movements discard the traditional all-out AMRAP (plus) sets. Instead, you will execute three strict, capped sets of 5 reps that scale in intensity week by week. This prioritizes flawless execution, builds massive neural power, and keeps your body fresh for the high-volume work that follows.\n\n2. BORING BUT BIG (BBB)\nFollowing your main strength work, you will transition into high-density 5x10 volume blocks using non-competing accessory lifts. This specific pairing allows one muscle group to fully recover while another is working, ensuring you accumulate maximum muscle-building stimulus in minimal time.\n\n3. HOURGLASS-BIASED ACCESSORIES & HIGH-DENSITY FINISHERS\nThe assistance work is engineered to develop a powerful V-taper, strong shoulder caps, a solid upper back, and exceptional glute and hamstring development. To completely eliminate dead time and fit the entire workout into a tight 60-minute window, isolation accessories leverage a high-intensity Extended Rest-Pause template: one heavy work set taken to failure, followed by brief micro-bursts of reps using deep breaths as the timer.\n\nTRAINING MAX - 90%\nThis program utilizes a training max for the main lifts. Take your current 1RM and multiply by 90%, then use that as your TM.\n\nPROGRESSION\nYou will run two consecutive 3-week waves before taking a formal deload. \n- Weeks 1–3 (Cycle 1): Establish baseline numbers with Block 1 main lifts.\n- Weeks 4–6 (Cycle 2): Increase TMs (Upper +5 lbs / Lower +10 lbs) and repeat the 3-week wave with the same lifts.\n- Week 7 (The Deload): Main lifts to 3 sets of 5 reps at a relaxed 40%–60% of your TM. Do not take anything to failure.\n- Weeks 8–13 (Block 2): Recalculate your percentages based on your current TMs and transition fully into the Block 2 main lift variations (Sumo Deadlift, Push Press, Leg Press, Incline Bench).\n- Week 7 (The Deload): Main lifts to 3 sets of 5 reps at a relaxed 40%–60% of your TM. Do not take anything to failure.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-27T21:38:01.062Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Lower: Deadlift & Legs","Upper: OHP & Back","Rest/Conditioning","Lower: Legs & Glutes","Rest/Conditioning","Upper: Back & Bench","Rest/Conditioning"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":70},{"r":5,"pct":80},{"r":5,"pct":90}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":7,"x":5}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":5}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":5}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":20,"hi":30,"rpe":7,"x":4}]}]}]}